<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Tervingi</h1><p class="st-meta">291 CE – 376 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gothic people north of the lower Danube whose flight from the Huns in 376 led to the Roman disaster at Adrianople.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Tervingi are first named in 291 as a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> living between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dniester">Dniester</a>, in former Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dacia">Dacia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-moldavia">Moldavia</a>. They emerged from the Gothic peoples who had raided the empire through the 3rd century and settled after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> abandoned Dacia around 271.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were ruled by tribal leaders under an overall judge (iudex), the best known being Athanaric. A treaty with Constantine in 332 made them Roman allies and opened trade. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> spread among them through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulfilas">Ulfilas</a>, who translated the Bible into Gothic, and Athanaric persecuted Christians in 369–372. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a> fought them in 367–369.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 376 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> attacked, and a large group under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fritigern">Fritigern</a> was admitted across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>. Roman mistreatment led to war, and in 378 they destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens's</a> army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edirne">Adrianople</a>. They later formed the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 291 CE – 376 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:65.49%;width:1.69%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>291 CE – 376 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Athanaric, Fritigern</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Gothic paganism; Arian Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gothic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>, <a href="/countries/moldova">Moldova</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Thervingi, Danubian Goths</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=334&amp;focus=tervingi" aria-label="Tervingi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5279 550 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tervingi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5599 806h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5599 806h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Romania. <a href="/atlas?year=334&amp;focus=tervingi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

